codex
The first false mutation was invalid as non-vacuity evidence: although it parsed and its proof exited nonzero, the backend stopped on an undecidable symbolic predicate before reaching the false result. Per the audit standard, I am not counting that. I’m replacing it with a ground mutation at the same entry state (`S = .PString`) so execution must reach the false `"!"` result obligation and fail there.
apply patch
