One further real-program boundary matters: the submitted Python is recursive while the canonical is iterative. I’m extending the differential evidence across CPython’s recursion boundary. This does not undermine the K reachability result itself, but it affects how broadly that result can be bridged back to actual Python execution and the prompt’s unrestricted string domain.
